> No need to do annoying analysis.

There's always a need for annoying analysis. :grin: 

This looks generally correct though well spotted. We should probably add `get_position()` in `VariantParser::Stream` so it is available for all derived classes, as this will occur for all, but that could be in a follow up.

The only bit I'm unsure about is:
```
uint64_t VariantParser::StreamFile::get_position() const {
	ERR_FAIL_COND_V(f.is_null(), -1);

	return f->get_position() - _get_buffer_remaining_length();
}
```
Not being someone who uses `FileAccess` much I don't know if `get_position()` is guaranteed to return the file length after EOF in all cases (I don't know what the contract here is, but I'll try and work out, you are probably ahead of me here). But if this is so, then the fix is fine.

If looks like `FileAccess` is inherited by a few classes, so we are relying on `get_position()` to return length when EOF. For safety (unless someone can confirm `get_position()`) is safe to use at EOF in all cases), we could try something like:
```
if (!f->eof_reached())
{
return f->get_position() - _get_buffer_remaining_length(); 
}
else
{
return f->get_length() - _get_buffer_remaining_length();
}
```
Again, I'm not sure if this is necessary, probably not, but just putting it out there.
